    "n1": {"x": 2350, "y": 0, "w": 400, "fill": "green", "text": "Design notes\n\n• Same family as Crossix and Bomb: cream glass, rounded numerals, the menu circle top right, Bomb's card rendering. Salad's own personality is the card table: every game screen sits on the room's table theme (default Classic Green Felt) and the house screens carry a felt-green accent.\n• Cards are original: rank and suit index top left, a large suit for pips, and simple line-drawn court figures (crown, tiara, cap) for K, Q, J in the suit's colour.\n• Turn state is never colour alone: the player to move has a ring in their colour plus a 'Playing' tag, the header says 'Your turn', and the status line names who is next.\n• Playable cards are lifted and bright; unplayable ones sit lower on a grey face and are disabled. The lead suit is named in the middle of the table.\n• Kitty (my call in the plan): leftover cards when the deal is uneven, turned face up for the first trick's winner.\n• Every text pairing measured with a script (166 pairs, all pass): 4.5:1 text, 3:1 marks and large numerals, light and dark.\n• Example game: 4 players, 1 deck, 1,120 points in all. Final: Sam 110, Alex 150, Brooke 415, Dana 445."}
  },
